      <section id="overview" class="card">
        <h3>What this is</h3>
        <p>
          Your EPK is a website designed to give promoters, bookers and venues
          one simple place to find your DJ information.
        </p>

        <div class="grid">
          <div class="mini-card">
            <h4>What it includes</h4>
            <p class="muted">
              Bio, mixes, press highlights, video, photos and booking contact.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="mini-card">
            <h4>Why it matters</h4>
            <p class="muted">
              A professional EPK makes it easier for promoters to understand your style
              and book you for events.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="how-it-works" class="card">
        <h3>How it works</h3>
        <p>Your EPK works using three simple parts:</p>

        <div class="grid">
          <div class="mini-card">
            <h4>1. Website structure</h4>
            <p class="muted">
              This controls the design and layout of your EPK. You own this code
              but you don't need to edit it.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="mini-card">
            <h4>2. Your content</h4>
            <p class="muted">
              Your DJ name, bio, links and videos are stored in one file called
              <code>data.json</code>.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="mini-card">
            <h4>3. Hosting</h4>
            <p class="muted">
              Hosting simply means putting your website online so people can visit it.
              We will use GitHub Pages because it is free and reliable.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="mini-card">
            <h4>Your website address</h4>
            <p class="muted">
              When first published your site will have a GitHub address.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <pre><code>yourusername.github.io/your-epk</code></pre>
        <p>You can also connect your own domain later for something more professional:</p>
        <pre><code>www.yourdjname.com/epk</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section id="github-explained" class="card">
        <h3>What is GitHub?</h3>
        <p>GitHub is a platform where developers store and manage projects.</p>
        <p>In this case GitHub will store your EPK website and publish it online.</p>
        <p>Think of GitHub as the place where your website lives and where you update your content.</p>
        <p>We will use GitHub for two things:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>storing the website files</li>
          <li>publishing the website online</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="github" class="card">
        <h3>Setting up GitHub</h3>
        <p><strong>Video walkthrough:</strong></p>
        <p class="muted">[Add how-to video link here]</p>
        <p>I recommend using Google Chrome for setup.</p>

        <ol>
          <li>Create a free account on GitHub</li>
          <li>Sign in to your account</li>
          <li>Go to the EPK template repository</li>
          <li>Click <strong>Use this template</strong></li>
          <li>Click <strong>Create new repository</strong></li>
        </ol>

        <p>This creates your own copy of the website inside your GitHub account.</p>
        <p>Inside the repository you will see all the files that make up your website.</p>
        <p><strong>Important:</strong> the only file you normally need to edit is <code>data.json</code>.</p>
      </section>

