        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="data-json" class="card">
        <h3>Understanding <code>data.json</code></h3>
        <p><strong>This is where all the magic happens.</strong></p>
        <p>The file <code>data.json</code> controls all the content on your EPK website.</p>
        <p>Instead of editing the website code you simply edit the information inside this file.</p>
        <p>The website then reads this file and displays the content on your page.</p>

        <p><strong>Video walkthrough:</strong></p>
        <p class="muted">[Add how-to video link here]</p>
      </section>

      <section id="technical-json" class="card">
        <h3>The technical part</h3>
        <p>
          This is the most technical step in the process — but don't worry,
          once you understand it the process is very simple.
        </p>
        <p>The <code>data.json</code> file is written in a format called JSON.</p>
        <p>JSON is structured using symbols like:</p>

        <pre><code>{
}
"
:
,</code></pre>

        <p>These symbols are important because they define the structure of the file.</p>
        <p>When editing the file we must be careful not to remove them.</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Do not remove brackets { }</li>
          <li>Do not remove quotation marks "</li>
          <li>Do not remove commas ,</li>
        </ul>

        <p>If these are removed the file will break and the website will not update correctly.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="json-structure" class="card">
        <h3>How JSON works</h3>
        <p>JSON is written in pairs:</p>

        <pre><code>keyword : content</code></pre>

        <p>Example:</p>

        <pre><code>"artistName": "KNAYOHMI"</code></pre>

        <p>The first part is the keyword. The second part is the content.</p>
        <p>You only edit the content. The keywords must stay the same because the website uses them to find the correct information.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="first-edit" class="card">
        <h3>Let's make our first edit</h3>
        <p>Now we will start editing the first section of the EPK.</p>
        <p>The header section controls:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>your DJ name</li>
          <li>your tagline</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This will be the first change that transforms the demo profile into your own EPK.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="header-edit" class="card">
        <h3>Editing your header</h3>
        <p>The header contains your DJ name and tagline.</p>

        <pre><code>"header": {
  "artistName": "KNAYOHMI",
  "artistTag": "South London DJ • House / Tech / Funk / Afro-Latin / Disco"
}</code></pre>

        <h4>artistName</h4>
        <p>Your DJ name.</p>
        <p>Example: <strong>DJ Luna</strong></p>

        <h4>artistTag</h4>
        <p>A short description of your style.</p>

        <p>Examples:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>London DJ • House / Disco</li>
          <li>Berlin DJ • Techno / Minimal</li>
          <li>Ibiza DJ • House / Tech House</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Keep this short and clear.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="hero-edit" class="card">
        <h3>Hero section</h3>
        <p>The hero section is the main introduction text at the top of your EPK.</p>

        <pre><code>"hero": {
  "title": "Keep it moving, keep it grooving.",
  "lead": "Groove-led, soulful and techy sets rooted in funk, disco, and house — built for connection, freedom, and letting go.",
  "pills": ["London, UK", "House / Disco / Afro-Latin Grooves", "Residencies + bookings"]
}</code></pre>

        <h4>title</h4>
        <p>A short statement describing your music.</p>
        <p>Example: <em>Dancefloor energy from start to finish.</em></p>

        <h4>lead</h4>
        <p>A short paragraph describing your DJ style.</p>

        <h4>pills</h4>
        <p>Small highlight tags displayed under your introduction.</p>

        <ul>
          <li>London, UK</li>
          <li>House / Tech House</li>
          <li>International bookings</li>
        </ul>

        <p>You can add or remove items inside the list.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="bio-edit" class="card">
        <h3>Bio section</h3>
        <p>The bio section allows you to store multiple versions of your biography.</p>
        <p>This is useful because different promoters request different lengths.</p>

        <pre><code>"bio": {
  "title": "Bio",
  "helpText": "Choose the version you need. Download as text in one click.",
  "versions": {
    "short": "Short bio text goes here...",
    "long": "Longer bio text goes here...",
    "full": "Full professional bio text goes here..."
  }
}</code></pre>

        <p><strong>Short bio</strong> – 1–2 sentences for quick introductions.</p>
        <p><strong>Long bio</strong> – one paragraph.</p>
        <p><strong>Full bio</strong> – longer biography for press or festivals.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="press-edit" class="card">
        <h3>Press section</h3>
        <p>This section highlights important events, residencies and appearances.</p>

        <pre><code>"press": {
  "sectionTitle": "Press & highlights",
  "residencyTitle": "Residencies",
  "residencies": [
    "STICKYJAM Music — South London Tech House Party"
  ]
}</code></pre>

        <h4>Residencies</h4>
        <p>Clubs or events where you regularly perform.</p>

        <h4>Appearances</h4>
        <p>Important events or gigs you have played.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="video-edit" class="card">
        <h3>Video section</h3>
        <p>This section introduces your DJ set video or showreel.</p>

        <pre><code>"video": {
  "title": "Video",
  "helpText": "Live clips and showreel."
}</code></pre>

        <p>Your video will normally be embedded from YouTube or Vimeo.</p>

        <p>Recommended content:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>DJ set recording</li>
          <li>Showreel</li>
          <li>Live performance clip</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="contact-edit" class="card">
        <h3>Contact section</h3>
        <p>The contact section allows promoters to book you quickly.</p>

        <pre><code>"contact": {
  "title": "Booking",
  "helpText": "Give me a message - I promise I won't bite!",
  "email": "hello@naomigabriel.com",
  "instagramUrl": "https://instagram.com/knayohmi",
  "soundcloudUrl": "https://soundcloud.com/knayohmi"
}</code></pre>

        <p><strong>Email</strong> – your main booking email.</p>
        <p><strong>Instagram</strong> – your main social profile.</p>
        <p><strong>SoundCloud</strong> – your mixes or music.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="tips" class="card">
        <h3>Important tips</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Only change text between quotation marks</li>
          <li>Do not remove commas</li>
          <li>Do not remove brackets</li>
          <li>Save the file before refreshing your website</li>
        </ul>

        <p>If something breaks, it is usually caused by a missing comma or quotation mark.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="json-example" class="card">
        <h3>Example JSON structure</h3>

        <pre><code>{
  "header": { ... },
  "hero": { ... },
  "bio": { ... },
  "press": { ... },
  "video": { ... },
  "contact": { ... }
}</code></pre>

        <p>Each section corresponds to a part of your EPK page.</p>

        <p><strong>Future improvement:</strong> you can also allow multiple videos using a structure like this:</p>

        <pre><code>"videos": [
  "youtube-link",
  "youtube-link"
]</code></pre>

        <p>This allows DJs to add more videos later without changing the code.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="faq" class="card">
        <h3>FAQ</h3>
        <p><strong>Can I use my own domain?</strong><br>Yes. You can connect your own domain later. You only pay for the domain name itself.</p>
        <p><strong>Do I need to edit code?</strong><br>No. Most users only need to update content in <code>data.json</code>.</p>
        <p><strong>Can I host it somewhere else?</strong><br>Yes. Because you own the files, you can host your EPK anywhere that supports static websites.</p>
      </section>

      <p class="footer-note">EPKLab setup guide · Free hosting via GitHub Pages · Built to be simple</p>
